.\" microdlnad man page
.TH microdlnad 8 "October 2012"
.SH NAME
microdlnad \- microDLNA DLNA/UPnP-AV Server
.SH SYNOPSIS
microdlnad options

.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
.B microdlna
is a lightweight but very functional DLNA/UPnP-AV server allowing easy 
sharing of your media files including pictures to any capable device or
client on your local wired and wireless network. Common PC software like 
totem is a good lightweight and fast choice for Linux/BSD; more fully
featured software for Linux, Windows and MAC is XBMC, also Mediahouse 
on Android, and any media sharing capable DVR/TV etc.

.SH OPTIONS
.PP
.B microdlna's 
options are normally set from the global /etc/microdlna.conf file.
.nf
But there may be times when you need to temporarily alter some of these options,
you can do this by running microdlna with the following command line switches.
.fi

Without \fB\-f\fR, no configuration file is read, not even /etc/microdlna.conf:
built-in defaults and command line options apply, and microdlna serves the
current directory ($PWD) as the user who started it.

.IP "\fB\-\-\fR\fIoption\fR\fB=\fR\fIvalue\fR, \fB\-\-\fR\fIoption value\fR"
Set any microdlna.conf option, overriding the file, e.g.
\-\-media_dir=V,/srv/videos \-\-db_dir= \-\-port=8201. '-' may be used
instead of '_' in option names. Giving \-\-media_dir, \-\-album_art_names or
\-\-network_interface replaces the values from the file; repeat the option
for several values.

.IP "\fB\-R\fR \fIRescan\fR"
This forces microdlna to rescan all of the media_dir directories.

.IP "\fB\-f\fR \fIconfig_file\fR"
Read this configuration file. Without \fB\-f\fR no file is read; the
microdlna service passes \fB\-f /etc/microdlna.conf\fR.

.IP "\fB\-p\fR \fIport\fR"
Run microdlna on this port exactly. Without a port, the first free port from
8200 upwards is used, and the default pid file is named microdlna-<port>.pid.

.IP "\fB\-w\fR \fIpresentation_url\fR"
Change the default presentation url address.

.IP "\fB\-d\fR \fIdebug\fR"
microdlna will run in the foreground with debug output.

.IP "\fB\-P\fR \fIpid_filename\fR"
Specify a location for the PID file.

.IP "\fB\-m\fR \fImodel\fR"
Force microdlna to report a specific model number.

.IP "\fB\-s\fR \fIserial\fR"
Force microdlna to report a specific serial number.

.IP "\fB\-t\fR \fInotify_interval\fR"
Change the notify interval, in seconds. Defaults to 895 seconds.

.IP "\fB\-h\fR \fIhelp\fR"
Show basic switch options for running microdlna.

.IP "\fB\-V\fR \fIVersion\fR"
Shows the program version number and exits.


.SH VERSION
This man page corresponds to microDLNA version 1.0.0

